= Proxy =

#type: node
#context: sop
#internal: a3ob_proxy
#tags: arma, p3d

"""Adds proxies (references to other .p3d files, such as weapon slots or seats) as packed primitives."""

A proxy marks a place where Arma puts another model, such as a weapon on a vehicle or a seat for a crew member. This node adds proxies to a LOD geometry.

With one input, the node adds a single proxy. With a second input, it adds one proxy for each point of that input.

@inputs

LOD geometry:
    Input 1.

Points (one proxy per point):
    Input 2.

@parameters

Path:
    #id: path

    The proxy model path, for example \a3\data_f\proxies\weapon_slots\top. Slashes become backslashes and a .p3d ending is removed.

    Type: Text. Default: (empty).

Common Proxies:
    #id: common

    Fill the Path from a list of common proxies.

    Type: Menu. Default: (choose).

    (choose):
        Sets this to (choose).

    Weapon: optic:
        Sets this to Weapon: optic.

    Weapon: pointer:
        Sets this to Weapon: pointer.

    Weapon: suppressor:
        Sets this to Weapon: suppressor.

    Weapon: magazine:
        Sets this to Weapon: magazine.

    Weapon: bipod:
        Sets this to Weapon: bipod.

    Driver: offroad:
        Sets this to Driver: offroad.

    Passenger: offroad:
        Sets this to Passenger: offroad.

    Gunner: hunter:
        Sets this to Gunner: hunter.

    Commander: hunter:
        Sets this to Commander: hunter.

    Light volume: car:
        Sets this to Light volume: car.

Index:
    #id: index

    The proxy number, 0 to 999.

    Type: Whole number. Default: 1. Allowed: From 0 to 999.

Number From Points:
    #id: autoindex

    With a second input: the first proxy gets Index, the next one Index + 1, and so on. Off: all get Index.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Translate:
    #id: t

    Where the proxy goes when there is no second input.

    Type: 3 numbers. Default: 0, 0, 0.

Rotate:
    #id: r

    Degrees. A proxy has no scale.

    Type: 3 numbers. Default: 0, 0, 0.

Orient From Points:
    #id: useorient

    With a second input: turn each proxy by the orient attribute of its point, if the point has one.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

The full page for this node is docs/user/reference/a3ob_proxy.html in the A3OB folder. Open it in a web browser.
